{"step_index":155,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:31:29Z","thinking":"**Defining the Scope**\n\nI'm currently focused on translating the business requirements document (BRD) into detailed specifications and user stories within a new document. My primary goal is to provide comprehensive, production-ready documentation that will be readily usable by the team, acting as both a Principal Product Manager and Systems Architect.\n\n\n**Structuring the Documentation**\n\nI've established the overall structure for the new documentation, which focuses on functional specifications and Agile user stories. I'm breaking everything down into Epics, and then, for each user story, I'm documenting the user story ID, title, format, priority, story points, business logic, technical implementation details, data contracts, edge cases, and acceptance criteria in Gherkin.\n\n\n**Detailing the Architecture**\n\nI'm now diving into the technical specifications, planning to document API contracts using REST/OpenAPI schemas, and core flows with Mermaid sequence diagrams. I'll also define state machines, status lifecycle diagrams, and telemetry/logging specifications. Remembering to create URL artifacts, I will use `gdocs mutate import-md` and format the document with the `bluedoc` preset. My goal is a comprehensive, deeply thorough document to aid development.\n\n\n**Outlining the Components**\n\nI'm now detailing the system architecture, creating a Mermaid diagram and specifying subsystems like the Web Chat UI, API Gateway, and Agent Orchestration Engine. I'm also specifying the WorkWeek HCM Adapter, ServiceImmediately ITSM Adapter, and the Policy RAG Vector Store. Further, I'm documenting the Dead-Letter Queue and Audit Logging Store.\n\n**Defining Data Contracts**\n\nI'm presently working on the global data contracts, which includes the `X-Authenticated-User` JWT claim schema, standardized API response envelopes, the error schema, and the `Idempotency-Key` protocol.\n\n**Formulating User Stories**\n\nI'm currently structuring Epics and breaking them down into Agile user stories. I've defined Epic 1, which centers on Identity Assertion, UI, and Session Management, including stories like \"Test Persona Selector,\" \"Multi-Turn Conversational Session Management,\" and \"Interactive Human-in-the-Loop Confirmation Cards.\" I am now beginning Epic 2.\n\n\n**Defining New Epics**\n\nI've just added several more Epics. Epic 3 focuses on the RAG engine for grounded policy Q&A, covering document ingestion, semantic retrieval, and domain containment. Epic 4 concerns Employee Self-Service, integrating with WorkWeek HCM. Epic 5 dives into Support Desk Management, incorporating ServiceImmediately ITSM functionality, and Epic 6 details resilient cross-system workflow orchestration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Detailed Functional Specifications and Agile User Stories document for HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"# Technical Specifications & Agile User Stories: HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)\\n\\n## Executive Summary & System Overview\\n\\nThis document provides the definitive **Functional Specifications, API Contracts, and Agile User Stories** for the engineering implementation of the **HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)**.\\n\\nThe solution enables employees to query internal HR policies and execute transactional self-service workflows across **WorkWeek (HCM)** and **ServiceImmediately (ITSM/HRSD)** through a unified conversational interface. All state-mutating transactions enforce mandatory **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) confirmation cards**, and multi-system workflows employ **Forward Escalation with Dead-Letter Queues (DLQ)** to guarantee data integrity.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. System Architecture & Component Interactions\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n    User([Employee / Chat UI]) -->|1. Prompt + Persona Switcher| Gateway[API Gateway & Auth Proxy]\\n    Gateway -->|2. Injects X-Authenticated-User JWT| Safety[Interaction Safety Interceptor]\\n    Safety -->|3. Validated Clean Intent| Orchestrator[Agent Orchestration Engine]\\n    \\n    subgraph Core_Services [Agent Platform Services]\\n        Orchestrator -->|Vector Search| VectorDB[(Policy Vector DB)]\\n        Orchestrator -->|Idempotent Tool Call| WW_Adapter[WorkWeek HCM Adapter]\\n        Orchestrator -->|Idempotent Tool Call| SI_Adapter[ServiceImmediately ITSM Adapter]\\n        Orchestrator -->|Log Event| AuditStore[(Audit & Log Store)]\\n        Orchestrator -.->|On Partial Failure| DLQ[(HR Operations DLQ / Event Bus)]\\n    end\\n    \\n    subgraph External_SaaS [Target Enterprise Systems]\\n        WW_Adapter -->|Service Credential + Scoped Token| WorkWeek[(WorkWeek Sandbox)]\\n        SI_Adapter -->|Service Credential + Caller Context| ServiceImmediately[(ServiceImmediately Sandbox)]\\n        VectorDB -.->|Scheduled Sync <= 1hr| DocRepo[(HR Policy Repository)]\\n    end\\n```\\n\\n### Component Responsibilities\\n\\n1. **Client Chat UI:** Web chat interface featuring conversational token streaming, a \n<truncated 26734 bytes>","Description":"\"Write comprehensive technical specs and user stories to scratch file\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/scratch/specs_user_stories.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing specs and user stories to file\"","toolSummary":"\"Write specs and user stories markdown\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
