{"step_index":186,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:37:14Z","thinking":"**Generate User Stories**\n\nI'm now focused on generating a dedicated markdown file, `user_stories.md`, specifically for user stories. The goal is a clean, standalone file in the artifact directory, formatted properly.\n\n\n**Craft User Story Document**\n\nI'm structuring the `user_stories.md` file now to include a document header with an agile overview, persona definitions (Employee, Manager, etc.), and a story point scale. I'm also planning a summary matrix, and I've started outlining the user stories, organized by epic. Epic 1 focuses on persona identity, and Epic 2 is about AI governance.\n\n\n**Detail User Stories**\n\nI've got the layout for the `user_stories.md` file set, and have moved on to detailing the specific user stories. I'm structuring these as Epic 3 for Policy Document Q&A, Epic 4 for Employee Self-Service, Epic 5 for Support Desk Management, and Epic 6 for Resilient Cross-System Workflow Orchestration. I'm following a standardized format for each story: persona, capability, and business value. I'll also add priority, MoSCoW prioritization, and story points to each one. There will also be some technical implementation notes and API considerations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Complete, standalone Agile User Stories and Acceptance Criteria document in Markdown format for the HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Agile User Stories & Acceptance Criteria: HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)\\n\\n**Product:** HR Agentic Virtual Assistant  \\n**Version:** MVP 1.0  \\n**Methodology:** Agile / Scrum  \\n**Target Release:** Q3 2026  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Persona Definitions\\n\\n| Persona Name | Role / Description | Primary Use Cases |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Jane Doe (Employee)** | Individual Contributor (Remote, Eng