{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:40:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-17T14:40:40Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-17T14:40:40Z\nFile Path: `file:///google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/gdrive/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 253\nTotal Bytes: 12088\nShowing lines 1 to 253\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: gdrive\n3: description: >-\n4:     List, search, upload, download, update, and manage Google Drive files and\n5:     folders using a Go CLI. Use when listing files, searching Drive, downloading\n6:     or uploading files, updating file content in-place, creating folders,\n7:     creating shortcuts, moving/copying/renaming files, sharing, managing permissions, viewing\n8:     revisions, exporting Google files, getting file URLs, or monitoring and\n9:     watching Drive activity for triggers. Don't use for editing\n10:     Docs/Sheets/Slides content (use those specific skills instead). Also use\n11:     when the user shares a drive.google.com URL.\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # gdrive\n15: \n16: ## Command Namespacing & Security\n17: \n18: To enforce robust agent safety boundaries and support prefix-based terminal\n19: command permission scopes, the `gdrive` CLI routes operations through dedicated\n20: `readonly` and `mutate` namespaces:\n21: \n22: -   **`readonly` namespace**: Applied to commands that strictly browse, search,\n23:     read, export, or audit Drive assets without modifying any remote state.\n24: -   **`mutate` namespace**: Applied to commands that upload files, edit content,\n25:     create folders, delete files, or manage sharing permissions in the cloud.\n26: \n27: AI agents MUST consistently use the namespaced subcommand structures shown below\n28: (e.g. `gdrive readonly ls` and `gdrive mutate upload`).\n29: \n30: -   **CXF-Delegated Impersonation**: Pass the global flag `--target_user <ldap>`\n31:     to act on behalf of another u\n<truncated 9728 bytes>\n                       : email)                                        :\n224: | `readonly permissions`       | List permissions                              |\n225: | `mutate remove-permission`   | Remove permission                             |\n226: | `readonly audit-permissions` | Recursive permission audit                    |\n227: | `readonly capabilities`      | List file capabilities (supports `--filter`)  |\n228: | `readonly recent`            | Recent files                                  |\n229: | `readonly starred`           | Starred files                                 |\n230: | `readonly quota`             | Show quota                                    |\n231: | `readonly revisions`         | List file revisions                           |\n232: | `readonly shared-drives`     | List shared drives                            |\n233: | `readonly tree`              | Display folder tree                           |\n234: | `readonly list-comments`     | List comments                                 |\n235: | `mutate add-comment`         | Add a comment                                 |\n236: | `mutate reply-comment`       | Reply to a specific comment thread            |\n237: | `mutate resolve-comment`     | Resolve a comment thread                      |\n238: | `mutate batch`               | Execute batch ops                             |\n239: | `readonly watch`             | Start a background watcher for Drive activity |\n240: \n241: ## Global Flags\n242: \n243: -   `--json` — output as JSON (works with all read commands)\n244: -   `--target_user <ldap>` — Act on behalf of the specified target user using\n245:     CXF-delegated impersonation (requires ssoproxy and appropriate\n246:     authorizations)\n247: \n248: ## Reporting Issues\n249: \n250: Report bugs or improvements for this skill at\n251: [Agent Skill: gdrive](http://b/hotlists/8078139). See the `skill_issue` skill\n252: for instructions on filing and triaging skill bugs.\n253: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
